From 7b9fc28fc60f2b827f5c2de7804e7a641d44fd62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FatBoy721 <203330788+FatBoy721@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:13:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] drm/apple: T6050 HDMI: set the fixed output up again
 after a system sleep

After an s2idle on the J714s with a display on the HDMI port the display
never comes back: at the wake DCP sees HPD high and connects, the DPTX
firmware reports link faults 22 and 24 on target 0:3 (no AUX),
dcp_dptx_connect() times out waiting for the port's link configuration,
and the same happens on every HPD cycle, an unplug and replug included,
until a reboot (betizzel/omarchy-m5#22, reproduced by TripleU613 on
v272-16 with a Samsung G9).

The HDMI route goes through the atc3 display crossbar, which shares the
ATC3 power domain. The sleep takes that domain down and the crossbar wakes
with its select register cleared, while the mux core still holds the
selection taken at probe. The driver has two ways of setting a route up
again after a sleep, and neither runs for this output:

- dcp_platform_resume() sets the fixed HDMI output up again
  (dcp_fabric_hdmi_reinit(): converter power, PHY, crossbar output
  deselected and selected again) only for external_native, the T6030 one;
- the H17P sleep path parks and unparks Type-C routes
  (dcp_typec_route_park()), and the fixed HDMI route is none
  (active_typec_route is NULL).

Nor does the crossbar driver restore its routes: apple_dpxbar_resume() is
T6030-only.

Run the fixed-HDMI re-setup for the T6050 external coprocessor's HDMI
output too. dcp_fixed_hdmi_sleeps() gates it on a fixed PHY with an HDMI
HPD GPIO on apple,t6030-dcpext (as before) or apple,t6050-dcpext, and
dcp_platform_resume() calls it for every DCP, a no-op elsewhere. On the
T6050 it sets the converter's power enables (already on) and deselects and
selects the crossbar output again, which rewrites the select register; the
Type-C mux step is skipped, as the J714s DP-only PHY has no mux (the
suspend's DPTX deactivate stops that PHY and the next activate starts it
again). It runs after the Type-C unpark and before the HPD sample that
connects the display again. Nothing changes at suspend: a T8142 crossbar's
deselect writes no register while the output's link is down, so there is
nothing to park. The M1/M2 Pro HDMI ports and the native external retry
(dcp_external_retry(), external_native only) are unchanged.

The "forwarding converter service requests" line missing after the wake
is a consequence, not the cause: dcp-hdmi.c logs it once per boot, and the
forwarder has nothing to do while the link does not train.

Compiles with W=1 without diagnostics on integration/aurora 677be395b9d2
with patches 0001-0020 (LLVM 23).

Tested on the owner's J714s (HP E240c at 1920x1080@60 on the HDMI port),
as this change ported onto the kernel it runs (an older integration/aurora
base, 3766943238bd, with the J714s HDMI DT and ATC3 usb-aon always-on):
- stock module: s2idle by systemctl suspend, keyboard wake: link fault 22
  twice, the port 0 link configuration timeout, link fault 24, HDMI-A-1
  disconnected; the issue as reported;
- with this change: two s2idle cycles, HDMI-A-1 connected 1 s after each
  wake, "HDMI: setting up the output again (after system sleep)" once per
  wake, no link fault; an unplug and replug after the wake connects in 2 s;
  a cold boot with the monitor attached shows the desktop; the internal
  panel and Wi-Fi come back as before.
Not tried: a USB-C display or dock across a sleep (the owner has neither).

Signed-off-by: FatBoy721 <203330788+FatBoy721@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c        |  8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
index 9f5e8fc2a2ad..848af7da0a96 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
@@ -1396,19 +1396,39 @@ void dcp_fabric_hdmi_resume(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 }
 
 /*
- * T6030 HDMI output: the ATC PHY that runs it as four-lane DP, and the
- * crossbar it goes through, are in power domains that system sleep may
+ * The fixed HDMI outputs whose PHY and crossbar sleep with their ATC power
+ * domain: the T6030 one, and the T6050 J714s one (dcpext3 through the atc3
+ * crossbar). On the T6050 the crossbar driver restores no route after a power
+ * loss (apple_dpxbar_resume() is T6030-only) and the H17P sleep path parks
+ * only Type-C routes (dcp_typec_route_park()), so after an s2idle the crossbar
+ * wakes with its select register cleared while the mux core still holds the
+ * selection: the next connect gets no AUX (link faults 22 and 24) until a
+ * reboot. The M1/M2 Pro HDMI ports keep their setup and are left alone.
+ */
+static bool dcp_fixed_hdmi_sleeps(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
+{
+	if (!dcp->fixed_phy || !dcp->hdmi_hpd)
+		return false;
+	return dcp->external_native ||
+	       of_device_is_compatible(dcp->dev->of_node, "apple,t6050-dcpext");
+}
+
+/*
+ * T6030 and T6050 HDMI output: the ATC PHY that runs it as four-lane DP, and
+ * the crossbar it goes through, are in power domains that system sleep may
  * switch off, losing their setup, and the converter is powered through
  * GPIOs. Set them up again as probe did: converter power on, the PHY taken
- * out of DP and back into it, and the crossbar output selected again if the
- * HDMI route holds it. No HDMI link is up when this runs.
+ * out of DP and back into it where a Type-C mux manages it (T6030; the T6050
+ * DP-only PHY is started again by the next DPTX activation), and the crossbar
+ * output selected again if the HDMI route holds it. No HDMI link is up when
+ * this runs.
  */
 static void dcp_fixed_hdmi_reinit_locked(struct apple_dcp *dcp, const char *why)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&dcp_typec_fabric_lock);
-	if (!dcp->external_native || !dcp->fixed_phy || !dcp->hdmi_hpd)
+	if (!dcp_fixed_hdmi_sleeps(dcp))
 		return;
 	dev_info(dcp->dev, "HDMI: setting up the output again (%s)\n", why);
 	if (dcp->hdmi_pwren)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 638021c4bb6b..65fadc8f7436 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -10967,9 +10967,11 @@ static int dcp_platform_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (dcp_is_external_h17p(dcp))
 		dcp_typec_route_unpark(dcp);
 	dcp_enable_typec_work(dcp);
-	/* The HDMI output's PHY and crossbar may have lost their setup in sleep. */
-	if (dcp->external_native)
-		dcp_fabric_hdmi_reinit(dcp, "after system sleep");
+	/*
+	 * The HDMI output's PHY and crossbar may have lost their setup in sleep
+	 * (T6030, T6050; a no-op elsewhere).
+	 */
+	dcp_fabric_hdmi_reinit(dcp, "after system sleep");
 	/* Before the HPD IRQ comes back: an edge from now on is replayed. */
 	if (dcp->hdmi_hpd_irq)
 		dcp_hdmi_unplugged_in_sleep(dcp);
-- 
