The J714s profile was measured on the 18-core M5 Pro. The 15-core M5 Pro
J714s has the same boot MPIDR and three clusters of five cores, and the
CPU inventory check refused it ("unsupported CPU inventory"), so it only
offered s2idle.

Take the inventory from the DT's CPU nodes, every one of which the boot
loader started: refuse more than the profile's count, and refuse a
possible mask that differs from the DT (nr_cpus or NR_CPUS clipping
would leave started cores out of the sleep). The loop that follows still
checks every core. On a part with fewer cores, s2idle stays the default
and deep sleep is offered by name: there a deep-sleep wake has been seen
to leave the PMP down (aurora-silicon/linux #3419).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
